# Git commits

When asked to commit, **never run `git commit` until the user confirms the message.**

1. Inspect the diff and draft a concise commit message (why, not what).
2. Show the proposed message and wait for explicit confirmation (or an edited message).
3. Only then stage and commit with the approved text.

Do not invent a message and commit in the same turn. Suggesting the message is fine; applying it requires confirmation.
